<p class="legal-date">Last updated October 28, 2026</p>

<p>We want everyone to be able to use 8bit.nyc. The pixel map is drawn on a canvas, so it is hard to use with a screen reader, but everything on it is also available in plain text.</p>

<h3>What works today</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Every event on the map is also in the list next to it (or in the tray on phones), with its title, time, place and a link, and works with a keyboard and a screen reader.</li>
  <li>The menus, filters, legal pages and contact form are regular buttons, links and form fields.</li>
</ul>

<h3>What we are still working on</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The easter eggs and the monster game are visual only.</li>
  <li>Some small pixel text has low contrast.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Tell us</h3>
<p>If something on the site does not work for you, email info@8bit.nyc with what you were trying to do and the device or assistive technology you use. We will reply and try to fix it, or send you the information another way.</p>
